From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: marty <marty@fyai.co.nz>
Date: Sun, 6 Sep 2026 14:17:02 +1200
Subject: [PATCH] RetroPlayer: add an FBO-backed render buffer and pool

The sysmem buffers cannot serve a hardware-rendering game client: the client
needs a framebuffer object to render into, not a CPU buffer to be uploaded.
CRenderBufferFBO owns a colour texture attached to the pool's framebuffer and
returns that framebuffer's name from GetCurrentFramebuffer(), which is what
IRenderBuffer::GetCurrentFramebuffer() is a pure virtual for.

Ported from garbear/xbmc retro-gl-v3 (lrusak), with four fixes:

- m_texId was never initialised, so the destructor called glDeleteTextures on
  an indeterminate name whenever a buffer was destroyed before Allocate().
- CreateTexture() called glGenerateMipmap() before glTexImage2D() and left
  GL_TEXTURE_MIN_FILTER at GL_LINEAR_MIPMAP_LINEAR with no mipmap chain, so
  the texture was incomplete and sampled black.
- Nothing attached depth or stencil. A 3D client - which is every client that
  wants a GL context - would have rendered without a depth test.
- The pool reported itself compatible with every render setting.
  CRPRenderManager::GetRendererForSettings() walks the buffer pools and takes
  the first compatible one, so that would have captured software clients too.
  It now answers no until Activate().

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>
